---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 31, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Evaluation Framework & Editorial Methodology — The HR Stack Guide"
  description="How The HR Stack Guide evaluates HR software: our standardized 4-pillar framework covering pricing transparency, global compliance, platform usability, and data verification."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-14">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
          <li><a href="/" class="transition hover:text-indigo-600">Home</a></li>
          <li aria-hidden="true" class="text-slate-300">&gt;</li>
          <li class="font-medium text-indigo-600" aria-current="page">Methodology</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        Evaluation Framework &amp; Editorial Methodology
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
      <section>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          At The HR Stack Guide, our mission is to provide objective, data-driven comparisons for founders,
          HR leaders, and People Ops executives. Our rankings and vendor matrices are based on a standardized
          4-pillar evaluation framework updated quarterly for 2026.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 1: Transparent Pricing &amp; Real Cost Structure</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          We break down base platform fees, per-employee-per-month (PEPM) pricing, hidden currency conversion
          markups, deposit requirements, and contract cancellation terms to calculate the true Total Cost of
          Ownership (TCO).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 2: Global Compliance &amp; Legal Infrastructure</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          For Employer of Record (EOR) and Global Payroll platforms, we verify owned-entity coverage vs.
          third-party partner network reliance, automated localized tax withholding, statutory benefits
          administration, and IP assignment protections.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 3: Platform Usability &amp; Integration Depth</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          We assess API ecosystem depth, native integrations with core HRIS/Accounting software (e.g.,
          QuickBooks, Xero, NetSuite), onboarding speed, and self-serve employee mobile access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Pillar 4: Data Verification &amp; Independence</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Our research combines direct platform testing, verified public documentation, statutory labor
          guidelines, and aggregated buyer feedback. Vendors cannot pay for higher rankings or altered
          performance scores.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          For questions regarding our testing criteria or data verification, contact our research team at
          <a href="mailto:research@thehrstackguide.com" class="font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:underline">research@thehrstackguide.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
